    "lawCode": "Add §238-a, RPT L",
    "lawSection": "Real Property Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S7811\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to amend the real property law, in relation to prohibiting the\nimplementation of electronic billing and/or payment of rent without\nthe tenant's consent\n\n\n PURPOSE :\nThis bill would prevent the use of an electronic billing system for\nrent payments without tenant consent.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\nThe bill adds section 238-a of the real property law, stating:\n\n1. A landlord shall not implement an electronic billing and/or payment\nsystem for rent without prior written consent of the tenant subject to\nsuch billing and/or payment of rent. A landlord shall not require the\nparticipation in an electronic payment system as a precondition of\nexisting property by a prospective tenant nor shall a landlord impose\npenalties, financial or otherwise or deterrents upon tenants who fail\nto consent to electronic billing and/or payment of rent.\n\n2. For the purposes of this section, \"landlord\" shall mean an owner,\nlessor, sublessor, assignee or other person receiving or entitled to\nreceive rent for the use of occupancy of any housing accommodation or\nan agent of any of the foregoing.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nMandatory use of electronic or internet billing for rent payments is\nan unjust and unacceptable demand to be placed on the elderly,\nindigent and others who may be intimidated and unable to utilize these\nsystems. This legislation would preserve the option of using an\nelectronic rent payment system should a tenant consent to using one,\nwhile eliminating the usage of them as a means to inconvenience and\nharass elderly and other tenants into vacating dwelling units.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\nNew bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
