    "lawCode": "Add §235-g, RP L",
    "lawSection": "Real Property Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S7811A\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\nAn act\nto amend the real property law, in relation to\nprohibiting the implementation of electronic billing and/or payment of\nrent without the tenant's consent\n\nPURPOSE:\nThis bill would prevent a landlord from mandating that tenants can\nonly pay rent through an electronic billing and/or payment system.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\nThe bill adds section 235-g of the real property law, stating:\n\n1. A landlord shall not require a lessee or tenant to use an\nelectronic billing and/or payment system as the only method for the\npayment of rent. A landlord shall not assess any fee or other charge\nfor a lessee or tenant that chooses not to use an electronic billing\nand/or payment system.\n\n2. Any agreement by a lessee or tenant of a dwelling waiving or\nmodifying his or her rights as set forth in this section shall be\nvoid as contrary to public policy.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nMandatory use of electronic or Internet billing for rent payments is\nan unjust and unacceptable demand to be placed on the elderly,\nindigent and others who may be intimidated and unable to utilize\nthese systems. This legislation would preserve the option of using an\nelectronic rent payment system should a - tenant consent to using one,\nwhile eliminating the usage of them as a means to - inconvenience and\nharass elderly and other tenants into vacating dwelling units.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\nNew Bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\nNone.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n\n",
